  "synthesis": {
    "description": "When the methanol or MTBE plant trips, runs at reduced rates or restarts, the plant contact sends a short notice to gas schedulers and commercial staff describing the cause, such as a boiler taken out or a broken compressor shaft, and the expected restart. Updates follow as the restart estimate moves, ending with a notice that the plant is up and making spec product. Schedulers use these notices to adjust the gas they nominate to the plant.",
    "steps": [
      "The plant goes down, cuts rates or plans a restart.",
      "The plant contact sends a notice with the cause and expected timing.",
      "Schedulers adjust gas nominations to the plant's expected burn.",
      "Updates are sent as the restart estimate changes.",
      "A final notice confirms the plant is producing spec product."
    ],
    "approach": "A standard outage notice form with fields for plant, status, cause, current rate, expected restart and expected gas use, sent to a fixed distribution list, so schedulers get the same facts in the same place each time.",
    "rationale": "The notices are short and repetitive. A fixed template ensures each one states the expected gas impact and restart time that schedulers need to rebalance nominations.",
    "artifact_type": "email_template"
  },
